<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Campaign</p><h1 class="enc-title">Liberation of Ethiopia (1941)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1941</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The liberation of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopia">Ethiopia</a> in 1941 was the defeat of Italian occupation forces by British and Commonwealth troops working with Ethiopian patriots during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a>. It ended the Italian occupation that had begun in 1936. Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haile-selassie">Haile Selassie</a> returned to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/addis-ababa">Addis Ababa</a> in 1941 and restored the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopian-empire">Ethiopian Empire</a>.</p></div>
